 "about_text": "Bel Ami is a contemporary art gallery in Los Angeles, founded in the summer of 2016 by Naoki Sutter-Shudo and Sabrina Tarasoff. The gallery operates from a space inside the Asian Center on N. Hill Street in Chinatown. Its program centers on emerging and mid-career artists working across painting, sculpture, ceramics, and mixed media, with a roster spanning Los Angeles, Europe, and Japan. Bel Ami has built a reputation for adventurous, often narrative or satirical bodies of work, exhibiting artists such as Guillaume Dénervaud, Olivia Hill, Ben Sakoguchi, and Soshiro Matsubara. The gallery is a regular exhibitor at international art fairs, including Frieze, Liste, FIAC, Paris Internationale, miart, and the Dallas Invitational, and its exhibitions have been reviewed in numerous art publications.",
